The in-repo reference implementation is `packages/reactor-api/src/graphql/analytics-subgraph.ts`, and it is worth reading before hand-rolling the express version: `AnalyticsSubgraph` takes the `IAnalyticsStore` off its `SubgraphArgs`, constructs `new AnalyticsModel(new AnalyticsQueryEngine(store))`, and then injects the context through `graphqlManager.setAdditionalContextFields({ dataSources: { db: { Analytics: model } } })` rather than through a per-request context callback. Same required path, supplied once at subgraph construction.

The library is documented as tested against Apollo Server 3 and 4; a fuller worked example lives in the MakerDAO-SES ecosystem-api repository.

Choosing the store: the academy snippet constructs the engine over `MemoryAnalyticsStore` imported from `@powerhousedao/analytics-engine-browser`. That class does not exist anywhere in the monorepo — `git grep MemoryAnalyticsStore` returns zero hits outside the academy docs — so the snippet cannot compile as written. Substitute `PostgresAnalyticsStore` from `@powerhousedao/analytics-engine-pg` for a Node/server process (this is what `reactor-api` itself does, even locally, where its `knex` handle is backed by PGlite), or `BrowserAnalyticsStore` from `@powerhousedao/analytics-engine-browser` when the engine runs in a browser. Any `IAnalyticsStore` satisfies `AnalyticsQueryEngine`, so the resolver wiring above is unchanged either way.

